body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in: 4.7.beta1, 4.6.2.stable

### System information

Godot v4.7.beta1 - Windows 11 (build 22621) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 31.0.101.4502) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1255U (12 threads) - 15.73 GiB memory - WASAPI (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)

### Issue description

When using a combination of a GridMap, MeshInstance3D and custom shaders, some parts of GridMap are displayed behind another mesh depending on camera angle.

<img width="1846" height="751" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edf26615-958a-4b7b-9a27-dfa68a909f6d" />

In example project, MeshInstance3D (y = -5) is located lower than GridMap (y = 0) and all of GridMap's cells are on floor 0. So I expect GridMap to be visible independent of camera angle.

I use quads as meshes for GridMap but it's reproducible with cubes as well. Shaders for both materials have to be setting alpha in order to reproduce.

I'm not sure if that is a bug, maybe I'm not expected to use shaders like that.

### Steps to reproduce

The setup is quite complicated, it's better to look at MRP

1. Place a MeshInstance3D and a GridMap on the scene
2. Change MeshInstance3D transform.y so it's below GridMap
3. Create a MeshLibrary with a single mesh, it has to use a ShaderMaterial that sets alpha:
```
shader_type spatial;
void fragment() {
	ALPHA = 1.0;
}
```
4. Populate GridMap with newly created meshes on floor 0
5. Set up MeshInstance3D to use a Quad mesh of a big size and a ShaderMaterial that sets alpha too:
```
shader_type spatial;
uniform sampler2D albedo_tex : source_color;
void fragment() {
	vec4 tex = texture(albedo_tex, UV);
	ALBEDO = tex.rgb;
	ALPHA = tex.a;
}
```
6. Add any texture in parameters of the shader above
7. Rotate the camera to see some parts of a GridMap being displayed behind another mesh

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

[bug-gridmap-rendering.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27339671/bug-gridmap-rendering.zip)
